
<section class="panel panel-pad"><span class="metric-icon tint-red"><x-icon name="envelope-simple" /></span><h2 class="section-title mt-5">Google setup</h2><p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-6">Enable Gmail API and register a confidential Web OAuth client. Keep its client ID and secret in server configuration. Register this exact callback:</p><p class="mt-4 break-all rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-xs">{{ config('mailbox.google_redirect_uri') }}</p><p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-6">Requested permissions: account identity, <strong>gmail.readonly</strong> and <strong>gmail.compose</strong>. Verified aliases are read through Gmail's supported read permission.</p><p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-6 text-slate-500">For external apps, restricted Gmail scopes require Google's applicable verification and server-data security assessment. Testing access is limited to allowed test accounts. Internal Workspace use remains subject to administrator policy.</p><a class="text-link mt-4 inline-block text-xs" href="https://developers.google.com/identity/protocols/oauth2/web-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google OAuth setup ↗</a><p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-6">Supported: the authenticated mailbox and verified send-as aliases. Gmail screen delegation, Google Groups and service-account domain-wide delegation need separate access arrangements and are outside this phase.</p></section>
